{"requests": [
 {"kind": "fits", "text": "ok so our ADK concierge bot for the hotel chain forgets everything the second a guest closes the chat. product wants it to remember room preferences, allergies, the 'last time you mentioned...' kind of stuff across visits. we're on Cloud Run + Vertex AI. also legal is breathing down my neck: guests must be able to say 'forget me' and it actually wipes, and anything older than 18 months should just age out. what's the sane way to wire this up? demo is Thursday"},
 {"kind": "fits", "text": "We have roughly 40k legacy documents from a manufacturing client: scanned maintenance PDFs (some are just photos of paper), Excel BOMs with merged cells everywhere, and CAD drawings exported as PDF/TIFF. Need to make all of it searchable for an ADK agent that answers technician questions. Critically, this is multi-tenant: client A's drawings can never show up in client B's answers. How should I structure ingestion, chunking and the index so tenant isolation is enforced at retrieval time and not just hoped for in the prompt?"},
 {"kind": "elsewhere", "text": "my agent's session state keeps blowing up — after like 30 turns the tool outputs in the context are huge and Gemini starts truncating or hitting token limits mid-conversation. how do i stop the in-session history from getting so big? it's all within one chat, I don't care about remembering anything after the user leaves", "needs_instead": "Help managing the context window within a single conversation: trimming or summarizing tool outputs and turn history, limiting token growth. It does not need long-term memory, document search, deletion or tenant isolation."}
]}
